{"availability":"available","full":"Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797","name":"kev-mirror-797","description":"High availability mirror and network topology specifications for jaredpalmer/kev","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-27T02:22:03Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:04:11Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://www.ai-hao123.com/yingxiao/subject-62889341.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:10.963Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:10.963Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:10.963Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:10.963Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Small Jev-like decision models you can train and run yourself.","Kev is a family of small decision models built on Qwen3.5 and Qwen3.8 and based on the architecture described in Jev's Architecture Unmasked. You can use the pretrained weights or train your own. The API matches TypeSafe's System One, so you can point their Python SDK at your local server."],"features":["Yes/no (noul), multiple-choice (choice) and rating (score) questions in one request. The questions share the text but can't read each other.","Calibrated probabilities by default: each checkpoint ships with a temperature fitted on held-out data.","Drop-in for Jev: the TypeSafe Python SDK works against a Kev server unchanged.","Four sizes, from a 0.8B that runs on a laptop to a 27B for a single data-centre GPU.","Fine-tune on your own labelled examples. A coding-agent skill runs the whole loop on Modal, from finding your questions to serving the result."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"75704807532990cc0b4ffde6467153dbdd7798b6df3cbda3f59c19fe6d94202e","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:11.052Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:11.052Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Small Jev-like decision models you can train and run yourself.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"To get an HTTPS endpoint instead of a local server, you don't need this repo, just a Modal account:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"If you use a coding agent, npx skills add jaredpalmer/kev@kev-deploy does the same and wires the URL into your code. skills/kev-deploy has the GPU and cost table.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Kev-9B needs about 17 GB of GPU memory and Kev-27B 55 GB of weights (about 66 GB with the batching buffers); under load Kev-27B is compute-bound, and a B200, H200 or H100 costs about the same per request.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"75704807532990cc0b4ffde6467153dbdd7798b6df3cbda3f59c19fe6d94202e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:11.053Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T22:04:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Shijiuwei/kev-mirror-797/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:11.057Z","hash":"75704807532990cc0b4ffde6467153dbdd7798b6df3cbda3f59c19fe6d94202e","originalBytes":52653,"storedBytes":52653,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["run","kev","model","kev-4b","runs","questions","one","base","jev","modal","kev-9b","test","own","question","same","each","python","state","text","training","gpu","kev-27b","score","choice","models","about","data","sources","against","jaredpalmer","new","option","tests","what","accuracy","per","api","instructions","noul","probabilities","server","typesafe","bf16","docs","kev-0.8b","type","weights","answers","bash","checkpoi